cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Astraeus in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "Astraeus: adversarial stress testing of off-world rover autonomy under unknown disturbance priors"
type: software
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-12
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/vineigenphase/Non-Trivial---Astraeus"
authors:
  - family-names: Vinujan
    given-names: S.
    email: svinujan10@gmail.com
keywords:
  - adaptive stress testing
  - importance sampling
  - distribution shift
  - lunar rover
  - terramechanics
  - autonomy validation
  - cross-entropy method
abstract: >-
  Astraeus simulates thousands of autonomous rover traverses under an eight-dimensional
  disturbance vector (soil, terrain, rocks, slope, illumination, dust), re-weights one
  defensive-mixture Monte-Carlo campaign under six competing environmental priors with
  explicit effective-sample-size and support-coverage gates, searches adversarially for
  the most plausible failures with the cross-entropy method, and renders every episode
  in a deterministic software renderer and a live WebGL world model.
